{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1556058","title":"16S rRNA sequences of cultured Bacteria from industrial wastewater samples (LEG225/LEG858:V3-V4; TPU-1/RTU-4: V1-V4)V1-V4)","description":"This BioProject contains 16S rRNA gene sequences obtained by Sanger sequencing of cultured bacterial isolates from activated sludge and treated wastewater of industrial wastewater treatment plants. The sequences were generated for the identification of presumptive Legionella isolates as part of the study \"Enhancing Culturability of Legionella spp. in Wastewater Samples via Temperature-Dependent Pre-Incubation\".Two primer pairs were used: the Legionella-specific primers LEG225 and LEG858 (Miyamoto et al., 1997), targeting the V3-V4 regions of the 16S rRNA gene, and the universal bacterial primers TPU-1 and RTU-4 (Funke et al., 2004), targeting the V1-V4 regions.The sequences were taxonomically classified using BLASTn against the NCBI nucleotide database. The dataset includes both confirmed Legionella spp. and isolates identified as non-Legionella bacteria. Notably, some isolates subsequently identified as non-Legionella bacteria grew on BCYE agar supplemented with L-cysteine but not on BCYE agar without L-cysteine.","center":"Leibniz University Hannover","data_type":"Targeted loci cultured","submission_date":"2026/11/03 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN64623217","MIMARKS Specimen sample from Caedibacter taeniospiralis","uncertain",null,"2024-06-10",2024,"DE",null,null,null,"unresolved",52.0,9.0,"Germany",null,"anthropogenic environment","wastewater treatment plant","activated sludge","conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical"],["SAMN64623218","MIMARKS Specimen sample from Caedibacter taeniospiralis","uncertain",null,"202